From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WS-B <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:02:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0982 redfin: Bluetooth nub properties + AppleOLYHAL (sweetbtnub)

Carry the D22AP /arm-io/uart1/bluetooth properties (raw bytes: 4-byte LE OSData, NUL-terminated OSData strings, as the iPhone X tree) on the "bluetooth" and
"marconi-bt" stand-in nubs (transport-encoding 3, transport-speed 3000000,
vendor 0x5ac / product 0x12a0, supported-profiles 0x2ffb, coex 2, compatible
"bluetooth,n88", local/bluetooth-address, empty voice-record) so bluetoothd
picks a transport; the function-* GPIO properties are left off (no GPIO nub
to point them at; /dev/btwake covers wake). sweetbtnub is now a bitmask:
1 "bluetooth", 2 "marconi-bt", 4 an empty AppleOLYHAL service (BlueTool
matches IOProviderClass AppleOLYHAL). Property reads on all three, and
user-client requests, are logged (IOUserClient.cpp). Default off.


---
